{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/1453815-sekhem-for-sorcerers-and-immortals","id":1453815,"title":"Sekhem for Sorcerers and Immortals","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-29T21:55:47-07:00","id":1453815,"title":"Sekhem for Sorcerers and Immortals","content":"So it occurred to me that I can't seem to find an explanation of what a Sorcerer or Immortal can do with raw Sekhem if they have access to it. Both edition established that it can be stolen in various ways from Arisen and of course Relics, but never really explained why you would want to. At least, not in first edition (granted, Immortals were never an intrinsic part of the setting until Dark Eras in First Edition and we barely knew what a sorcerer even was (again, until Dark Eras)). And I can't seem to find any explanation of their abilities in second edition, though I don't know that one as well. Sorcerers use pillar points to augment their magic, not Sekhem itself, and Immortals have a rating in Sekhem but otherwise don't seem to use it directly as far as I can tell. And Sekhem doesn't drop for Immortals like it does for Arisen, so there isn't an inherent obvious benefit for harvesting it in the system. I could make things up, obviously (like &quot;Sekhem removes the need to meet any ritual components of a sorcerer's rite rather than just one of the three like a pillar point does&quot; or &quot;Sekhem allows whatever immortality maintenance ritual the Immortal has to perform to succeed automatically&quot;) but I feel like I might very well have missed an important piece of information somewhere in here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-29T21:58:43-07:00","id":1453816,"title":"","content":"Okay, thinking about it there are a few examples I can name. Last Dynasty and the Strangers use Sekhem to maintain their longevity and physical strength specifically without any &quot;inbetween&quot; rituals like blood bathing or Purification. And of course you can feed a hungry Amkhata servant. Anything else they can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T15:59:08-07:00","id":1454102,"title":"","content":"There is a sidebar on page 257 that explains what Immortals can do with Sekhum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}